<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Figueres Ferrer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1906–1990</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Figueres Ferrer was a Costa Rican politician who led the victorious side in the civil war of 1948 and then headed a governing junta for eighteen months. His junta abolished the army, nationalised the banks and extended full voting rights to women and Afro-Costa Ricans. He founded the National Liberation Party and was elected president twice, in 1953–1958 and 1970–1974.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-figueres-ferrer.jpg" alt="José Figueres Ferrer" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:MadriCR · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Figueres_Ferrer_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
